     iiddeenntt — identify RCS keyword string in files

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     iiddeenntt [--qq] [--VV] [_f_i_l_e _._._.]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The iiddeenntt utility searches for all instances of the pattern ‘$keyword:
     text$’ in _f_i_l_e_s.

     If no arguments are passed, then iiddeenntt parses the standard input.

     _k_e_y_w_o_r_d must only be composed of alphanumeric values in the C locale,
     followed by ‘:’ and a space.

     These options are supported:

     --qq   Quiet mode: suppress warnings if no pattern found.

     --VV   Do nothing, added for compatibility with GNU ident.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The iiddeenntt utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

